# Build context: repo root (ExxerCube.Prisma/).
# These exclusions keep the Docker build context small and prevent secrets/build
# artifacts from leaking into images.

# MSBuild output directories (host artifacts live outside the repo on E:\, but
# any local bin/obj dirs inside the tree are excluded for safety).
**/bin/
**/obj/

# Test assets and fixtures that are not needed in production images.
**/TestAssets/
**/Fixtures/
# Exception: the Web.UI document-processing demo bakes the PRP1 fixture set into
# the image (see Web.UI/Dockerfile). Re-include ONLY that subtree (GH#23): descend
# into Prisma/Fixtures, re-exclude every sibling, then re-include just PRP1. Without
# the `Prisma/Fixtures/*` re-exclude, `!Prisma/Fixtures/` drags the whole ~78M tree
# (PRP2, PRP1_Degraded/Enhanced) into the build context.
!Prisma/Fixtures/
Prisma/Fixtures/*
!Prisma/Fixtures/PRP1/
!Prisma/Fixtures/PRP1/**

# Git history
.git/
.gitignore
.gitattributes

# CI / IDE metadata
.github/
.vs/
.vscode/
*.user
*.suo

# Local secrets and overrides (never bake into images).
**/appsettings.Development.json
**/appsettings.Local.json
**/secrets.json

# Python source trees (not needed by .NET images; reduces context size significantly).
Prisma/Code/Src/Python/

# Node / npm (Playwright, coverage tooling)
node_modules/
**/node_modules/

# Coverage and test reports
coverage/
TestResults/
*.trx
*.coverage

# Documentation and planning (not needed in image)
docs/
scripts/
tools/
